    "• micaGO runs no cloud server — you use your own Firebase project.\n• Firebase is only for Android FCM push and the optional public-URL discovery.\n• Windows clients use WebSocket + local notifications while running. Huawei/HarmonyOS Push is deferred. iOS push is out of scope.\n• Firebase NEVER stores message content, contacts, phone numbers, bearer tokens, attachments, chat history, the device registry, or sync rules.\n• FCM payloads are transient delivery data. Message history still syncs over your normal micaGO connection." : {
      "comment" : "A description of Firebase setup for push notifications.",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true
    },
